    "sha": "97f4900e057c84f146edfdabe35ff8d59c314809",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKDk3ZjQ5MDBlMDU3Yzg0ZjE0NmVkZmRhYmUzNWZmOGQ1OWMzMTQ4MDk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T23:59:56Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-25T23:59:56Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): Heidenhain DIN/ISO stops for a manual tool change\n\nOn a machine that states tooling.tool_change = \"manual-retract-top\"\n(the Fehlmann Picomax 55, iTNC 530), the DIN/ISO post now writes, at\neach tool change: G00 G90 Z+0 M92 under the old tool call, the\noperator checks, M6 (MP 7440 bit 0 = 0 halts there), then the new T\nblock. The first tool gets the checks and M6 only.\n\nNew engine law: a script on a manual tool change machine must declare\nthe mode in manualToolChange, or the engine refuses the pair by name\n(post and machine) before any hook runs. heidenhain.cps and\nheidenhain-klartext.cps declare manual-retract-top.\n\nFixes #4085\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
