        "date": "2026-11-26T06:01:58Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): DIN/ISO manual change only on the verified installation\n\nThe #4114 review: the M92 retract and the M6 stop are safe only with the\nmachine parameters of the verified installation. The DIN/ISO post now\nrefuses by name each manual-retract-top machine that is not the Fehlmann\nPicomax 55 with iTNC 530 NC 340490-03 (the same check as the Klartext\npost). M0 now follows M6, so the halt does not depend on the M06 machine\nparameter, and on the Picomax the drives are off at the install stop.\n\nPinned by din_iso_refuses_a_manual_change_machine_it_was_not_verified_for\nand din_iso_retracts_and_stops_before_the_second_tool_moves (golden\npicomax_two_tools.nc: one M0 block for each change).\n\nFixes #4085\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
